23 CD GOV-017 m=M k=W c=M | Stop the Reserved part and continue only with compliant non-Reserved work (GOV-017); remainder: the request is issued through architecture-decision.
  x: Reserved decisions are requested with the architecture-decision Decision Request
  s: A one-line approval question in chat satisfies GOV-017 but not M's workflow.
24 UN m=U rel=GOV-017 | Reported ambiguity: whether an explicit approval in the original request of a headless run allows a Reserved change, given CLAUDE.md:138 ('an explicit user instruction counts as approval') and CLAUDE.md:139-141 ('in an autonomous or headless run, never make a Reserved decision').
  r: the two sentences conflict for pre-approved Reserved changes in headless runs; the source does not resolve precedence (Step-1 UNRESOLVED queue item)
  fhd: Whether an explicit approval contained in a headless run's original request authorizes a Reserved change.
25 CD GOV-017 m=M k=W c=M | An explicit user instruction counts as approval (GOV-017 explicit approval); remainder: it must be recorded through the architecture-decision workflow.
  x: approvals (incl. explicit instructions in the request) are recorded through architecture-decision
  s: User explicitly instructs adding a second DbContext; agent implements without a decision record: GOV-017 satisfied; M requires the record.
26 CD GOV-017 m=MN k=W c=M | Headless runs must not silently alter architecture (GOV-017); M says never make a Reserved decision in a headless run, proceed only on compliant paths and report every unresolved Decision Request.
  x: in headless runs no Reserved decision at all, plus an explicit report of every unresolved Decision Request
  s: A headless run that records an approved-in-prompt Reserved change transparently: arguably compliant with GOV-017 (not silent); M forbids making it.
27 XW m=MN fa=FC c=M rel=GOV-017 | Facet: in a headless run the agent does not wait for a decision response, even when no compliant work remains; it continues with the 'Proceeding with' work and reports. Clarifies the timing of the target obligation; relative to the oracle the no-waiting rule is a workflow constraint GOV-017 does not state.
  s: A headless run whose 'Proceeding with' is 'nothing' pausing for an approval that cannot arrive: not addressed by GOV-017; forbidden by M.
